    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0188" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg154"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 636.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 626 of February 1,
                    concerning the cases pending on October 16, 1896, before the American consular
                    court in Madagascar, I have to report that I am in receipt of a note from Mr.
                    Hanotaux stating in reply to an inquiry from this embassy that the instructions
                    of the minister of colonies to the French resident-general are to the effect
                    that all facilities should be given to the consuls for settling the cases
                    brought before their courts before the above-mentioned date of October 16,
                    1896.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith a copy and a translation of Mr. Hanotaux’s note.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d148-a1.xml" xpointer="d148-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
